    </edge>
    <edge source="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">The issuance of the Master Group Policy to the employer establishes the foundation for the policy’s provisions, including the availability of accelerated benefits with actuarial discounts outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c" target="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7">
      <data key="d3">The issuance of the Master Group Policy to the employer establishes the legal and operational foundation that permits timely beneficiary modifications through HR, ensuring continuity and adaptability in benefits administration.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">The master policy issued to the employer includes a total benefit pool of $280,000, and the maximum allowable acceleration of benefits under its terms is capped at $250,000, making this restriction applicable to the overall coverage provided.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c" target="6158d9a5-ff94-4835-99aa-58729bb45911">
      <data key="d3">The master policy issued to the employer establishes the foundation for coverage, while the beneficiary allocation rule ensures equitable distribution when multiple parties are named, directly influencing how benefits from the policy are paid out.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c" target="22c4b994-6a5b-49d5-a129-731be848f272">
      <data key="d3">The issuance of the Master Group Policy to the employer enables the administration of benefits, including timely payouts such as those described in fact_sentence_2, ensuring claims are processed efficiently once documented.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The employer holding the Master Group Policy enables the administration of benefits, which includes directing claims submissions to the proper department—Alliance Group Benefits—as outlined in the procedural guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
