    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="704873e4-f362-4a71-8e40-cfdd3ea1f5e2">
      <data key="d3">Even though the employee chose supplementary coverage, such choices are subject to final authority under the Master Policy in cases of inconsistency.</data>
      <data key="d4">superseded by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">If there is a conflict between the certificate and the Master Policy, the latter takes precedence over the specified beneficiary, potentially invalidating or modifying the primary beneficiary status.</data>
      <data key="d4">modified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">If the Master Policy contradicts the stated payout rule, it supersedes the provision granting 100% to the primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">supersedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy overrides the certificate when conflicts arise, establishing its supremacy in interpreting terms and conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">preempts</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">Since the Master Policy holds ultimate authority over the certificate, its issuance to the employer ensures consistency and control over contractual interpretations when conflicts occur.</data>
      <data key="d4">controlled by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">The master policy takes priority if its terms contradict the certificate, ensuring consistency in interpretation. This supremacy means all aspects of coverage—including benefits, limitations, and eligibility—are defined by the master policy’s framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">supersedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="1976d0c5-bd83-492b-af9c-24b53a14f5dc">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the Master Policy as supreme in cases of inconsistency, thereby limiting the authority of the certificate. However, fact_sentence_2 affirms that the certificate remains legally operative under its own terms unless contradicted by the higher-level policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">supersedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07">
      <data key="d3">The maximum voluntary coverage limit depends on the employee’s salary and must align with the terms set forth in the overarching Master Policy, which takes precedence over this certificate.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the legal priority of the Master Policy over this certificate, meaning any provision like the terminal illness acceleration described in fact_sentence_2 must align with master policy rules.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The master policy's supremacy ensures rules about accelerating benefits — like reduced payouts — are enforced consistently across certificates.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
      <data key="d3">The clause about the Master Policy controlling resolves jurisdictional disputes, which may affect how provisions like the $5,000 minimum acceleration are interpreted or enforced across different documents.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7">
      <data key="d3">The master policy supersedes the certificate in disputes, potentially affecting how beneficiary changes are processed under its authority. However, the ability to update beneficiaries remains functional regardless of such hierarchies.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy’s supremacy over the certificate implies it may enforce the $250,000 cap on benefit acceleration, ensuring consistency across policies regardless of individual certificate details.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The clause stating the Master Policy overrides the certificate ensures that institutional guidelines govern disputes, which includes directing claims to the proper department as outlined in the secondary statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
