    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy governs the application and limits of the $280,000 coverage amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy includes provisions governing the $100,000 voluntary coverage, ensuring it aligns with overall plan rules and eligibility criteria.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="704873e4-f362-4a71-8e40-cfdd3ea1f5e2">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that all coverage follow the Master Policy's terms means any voluntarily elected coverage must comply with those established conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy governs the implementation timeline of coverage, ensuring that the effective date—June 1, 2024—is formally recognized and applied consistently across policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="c640c250-030a-4238-b2c4-ee2b7b8201bf">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for the employer to pay premiums for basic coverage arises from the terms outlined in the Master Policy, which governs all aspects of the plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy establishes the rules governing who may be named as a beneficiary, such as Jordan Casey Taylor.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy governs all aspects of coverage, including how beneficiary designations like that of Jordan Casey Taylor as spouse are enforced and interpreted.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy sets the conditions under which the primary beneficiary receives 100% of the benefit, ensuring compliance with contractual obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="52b0c634-376a-4bbe-a0e1-f374e691f95a">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy governs all aspects of coverage, including defining who qualifies as a contingent beneficiary such as the Taylor Family Revocable Trust.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="0fd4ce41-df87-49ef-b846-edcb6c8e3ffc">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy establishes the framework under which the contingent beneficiary is entitled to receive 100% of the benefit payout upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">enforces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The applicability of the Master Policy’s rules—including limitations and requirements—is predicated on the existence of a documented certificate confirming coverage under that same policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">Since coverage is bound by the Master Policy’s terms, its legal and operational framework originates from the policy being formally issued to the employer, establishing authority and scope.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88">
      <data key="d3">Because the master policy governs all conflicts, the certificate’s validity and scope depend entirely on the master policy’s stipulations, making compliance mandatory regardless of wording in the certificate itself.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5" target="5cd717d1-9c10-4167-8667-538fce460dac">
      <data key="d3">The condition under which coverage applies—the Master Policy—is relevant only after eligibility has been established. Thus, the existence of eligibility from the start of employment enables the enforcement of policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
