      <data key="d3">The existence of standard terms and conditions in the certificate governs all aspects of coverage, including optional benefits like supplemental coverage. However, it does not specify how those options are structured.</data>
      <data key="d4">subsumes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1976d0c5-bd83-492b-af9c-24b53a14f5dc" target="a1425e35-53a8-4ea3-8514-eaefbb3dc8bd">
      <data key="d3">The term "subject to the terms" implies that rules like rounding the benefit amount apply under the policy's formal provisions. This suggests the rounding practice aligns with documented policy language.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1976d0c5-bd83-492b-af9c-24b53a14f5dc" target="ebda2a4b-af98-4477-809f-34d2ba734e4c">
      <data key="d3">The terms of the certificate govern how benefits are adjusted; specifically, salary changes lead to a recalculation of the basic benefit amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1976d0c5-bd83-492b-af9c-24b53a14f5dc" target="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07">
      <data key="d3">The limitation on voluntary supplemental coverage—capped at five times the employee's salary—is part of the broader set of terms and conditions outlined in the insurance certificate.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1976d0c5-bd83-492b-af9c-24b53a14f5dc" target="ffc538ab-5ff6-4960-b2c1-1eef9713da66">
      <data key="d3">Sentence 1 establishes that the policy operates under defined terms, one of which may include the method used to calculate benefits. Sentence 2 specifies that the basic benefit is determined by multiplying the annual base salary by two—this detail would typically appear within the terms mentioned in sentence 1.</data>
