    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">Understanding that the total coverage includes $100,000 in voluntary portions makes sense when considering it's available in $10,000 increments, supporting the feasibility of reaching that exact amount through multiple elections.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The ability to select coverage in $10,000 increments enables an employee to reach exactly $100,000 in voluntary supplemental coverage by choosing ten such units.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="704873e4-f362-4a71-8e40-cfdd3ea1f5e2">
      <data key="d3">The availability of elective coverage in $10,000 increments makes it feasible for the employee to select a specific amount, such as the $100,000 chosen here.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="c0378a0c-15e9-46db-80c6-212e4003560d">
      <data key="d3">Voluntary coverage is offered in $10,000 blocks, so the $12 monthly charge aligns with one such block based on the employee’s election.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The ability to elect voluntary coverage in $10,000 increments enables the issuance of certificates like this one, confirming such coverage under the master policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">Employees’ ability to elect voluntary supplemental coverage in $10,000 increments depends on the existence of a master policy issued to the employer, which governs the overall structure and eligibility rules.</data>
      <data key="d4">required by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">The ability to elect voluntary coverage in $10,000 increments is a detail contained within the broader contractual framework established by the Master Policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="1976d0c5-bd83-492b-af9c-24b53a14f5dc">
      <data key="d3">Supplemental coverage may be selected in $10,000 increments, a structural rule that falls under the umbrella of the overall policy terms described in the certificate.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523" target="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07">
      <data key="d3">The incremental election method allows employees to choose coverage in $10,000 steps, while the maximum allowable amount is capped at five times their salary, ensuring choices remain within defined financial limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
