    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">The maximum possible supplemental coverage—limited to five times the employee’s salary—is a key factor determining how high the total coverage can go; if the employee earns less than $20,000 annually, the $100,000 supplemental amount would exceed the allowed limit.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The maximum allowed voluntary supplemental coverage—set at five times the employee’s salary—is relevant because it determines whether the actual $100,000 coverage is permissible under company guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="704873e4-f362-4a71-8e40-cfdd3ea1f5e2">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a maximum voluntary coverage limit set at five times the employee’s salary explains why the chosen supplemental amount could have been selected under established guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="c0378a0c-15e9-46db-80c6-212e4003560d">
      <data key="d3">While the maximum voluntary coverage is limited to five times the employee’s salary, the actual premium paid—$12 per month—is determined independently based on the selected coverage amount and other factors like age and health.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The upper limit on voluntary supplemental coverage—five times the employee’s salary—is relevant because it determines the extent of coverage reflected in the certificate serving as proof of benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs certificate</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">The rule limiting voluntary supplemental coverage to five times the employee’s salary establishes a quantifiable boundary for personal choices under the group policy. This constraint operates within the broader system where the employer holds the master policy, ensuring consistency across participant enrollments.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88">
      <data key="d3">Since the Master Policy governs in case of conflicts, the $100,000 supplemental coverage must comply with its rules—including limits like five times the employee’s salary—to remain valid.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">The cap on voluntary supplemental coverage—five times the employee’s salary—is determined by the rules outlined in the Master Policy referenced in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="1976d0c5-bd83-492b-af9c-24b53a14f5dc">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that voluntary coverage cannot exceed five times the employee’s salary is included among the terms and conditions specified in the certificate.</data>
      <data key="d4">encompassed by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="5cd717d1-9c10-4167-8667-538fce460dac">
      <data key="d3">The cap on voluntary coverage being tied to salary implies that only those eligible from hire onward can have their coverage calculated relative to their earnings.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="f15e476d-3d7a-4b13-809d-10b26b7c85b3">
      <data key="d3">The cap on voluntary coverage being tied to salary means that timely enrollment (within 31 days of hire) is necessary to access up to the full potential amount allowed under the plan's rules.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="ffc538ab-5ff6-4960-b2c1-1eef9713da66">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the upper limit for optional coverage (up to five times salary), which helps frame the scope within which the basic coverage (two times salary) operates, providing comparative context for the overall benefit structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="ea7a7c5a-46ee-4c49-9178-8b7d77c3e523">
      <data key="d3">The maximum elective coverage being limited to five times the employee’s salary constrains the possible amounts that can be chosen in $10,000 increments under the voluntary plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c5f8925f-a280-4bc9-8813-a9b5d6d07c07" target="ebda2a4b-af98-4477-809f-34d2ba734e4c">
      <data key="d3">The maximum voluntary supplemental coverage depends on the employee's salary, which also triggers adjustments to the basic benefit amount upon change.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
