    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="551c8612-0cad-4d79-9420-0ec74b56d877">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="b4184af1-cb70-4ba0-850e-1a108667f24c">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="9cdf8bcb-8e3c-431b-8c67-1b742b95bcde">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="eb6f7412-9920-4875-a657-6278ce447960">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">amount</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="cd6b4b63-f16e-4ea4-abd2-4de023297e44">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="c43c5b16-b993-4f88-8cc9-12cd43b8f61d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="aa085081-2a0d-4445-a5d2-626a1a82cf31">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million cap sets the maximum allowable coverage, within which participants can elect additional amounts in $10,000 increments.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">The annual recalculation of the basic benefit is limited by the $1 million cap, ensuring that even if salary increases justify higher coverage, it cannot exceed this maximum threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="832e18bd-3db9-4b0d-a12a-09f2d351cc74">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million cap limits the maximum possible benefit that could result from salary-based recalculations. Without this ceiling, higher salaries might lead to unbounded increases in coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million cap limits how much coverage any participant can have, regardless of salary; therefore, even if someone earns enough to qualify for more than $1M via the "five times salary" rule, the actual coverage is capped at $1M.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million coverage cap sets the maximum allowable benefit level that applies when converting group coverage into an individual policy. This ensures that even though the new policy is issued at the employee's current age, it remains bounded by the prior group limit.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million cap defines the maximum possible coverage that could be eligible for porting after leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to constraints</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million cap ensures that any ported coverage remains within legally and contractually permissible limits, preventing over-insurance beyond the stated ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million cap on total group coverage sets the upper bound for any individual's benefit, which determines the maximum possible amount eligible for conversion into an individual policy under the specified terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million coverage cap ensures that even if someone qualifies for portability, their converted policy cannot exceed this limit. This restriction applies regardless of when the application is made during the 31-day period.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million coverage cap sets the maximum benefit level that determines the scope of any portable policy. Premiums for such policies are determined using age-based group rates applicable within that capped framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The $1 million coverage cap sets the upper bound for total group benefits, which indirectly shapes the maximum amount available for conversion or portability. This constraint ensures that even if someone qualifies for portability, they cannot transfer more than their prior group limit allows.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb33b086-526d-430a-ad69-e9ecec60f094" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
    </edge>
