    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">Election of additional coverage in $10,000 increments is permitted only up to the $1 million overall limit established by the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">operates within</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">The ability to elect additional coverage in $10,000 increments is subject to a hard upper limit defined by the employee’s salary, ensuring that total elective coverage cannot exceed five times their earnings.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">Election of incremental coverage during employment enables participants to increase their protection levels prior to leaving. This enhanced coverage level becomes eligible for porting into an individual policy upon termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The option to elect additional coverage in $10,000 increments directly influences the maximum amount that can be maintained when converting or porting coverage after leaving the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">Election of additional coverage in $10,000 increments affects the potential size of ported coverage, which is subject to age-banded group rates determined at time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 enables future expansion beyond the current $280,000 coverage outlined in fact_sentence_1, providing flexibility for participants to enhance their benefits incrementally.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables expansion</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The ability to select additional coverage in $10,000 increments enables employees to achieve the $100,000 voluntary coverage specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The option to add coverage in $10,000 increments presupposes that coverage has already begun; therefore, it relies on the effective date established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f9ed21b9-d1b4-4527-ace3-427b54952015" target="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">can be elected in increments of</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4fe26cb0-35b6-43c8-a6b8-de07c8738c10" target="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">can be elected in increments of</data>
    </edge>
