      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="a5008f6e-f8be-49dc-a3db-c5381c59bd04">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="c6884895-4f9c-4453-ab1e-721fbb4304bc">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">Coverage based on five times salary acts as a dynamic component determining individual limits, but it cannot override the fixed $1 million maximum set by the overarching policy restriction.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrained by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4">
      <data key="d3">The five-times-salary cap on elective coverage determines the maximum amount one can add through incremental elections, thereby limiting the practical scope of choosing additional coverage in $10,000 steps.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="832e18bd-3db9-4b0d-a12a-09f2d351cc74">
      <data key="d3">The maximum elective coverage is capped at five times the employee’s current salary, ensuring alignment with ongoing compensation levels. This rule enables fair and updated benefit calculations each year.</data>
      <data key="d4">enforces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">The maximum elective coverage is capped at five times the employee’s salary, and this cap is adjusted annually during the policy anniversary when the basic benefit is recalculated.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">The salary-based cap on elective coverage sets the upper bound for potential benefits, which informs the scope of protection available when converting to an individual policy after termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">The maximum coverage amount, capped at five times an employee’s salary, determines the upper bound of what can be converted into an individual policy upon leaving the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions conversion</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">The maximum elective coverage, capped at five times an employee’s salary, determines the upper bound of what can be converted into an individual policy during the transition window after leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The maximum coverage allowed under the group plan depends on the employee’s salary, influencing the potential benefit level available upon departure. This determines the extent of coverage that could potentially be ported after leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The maximum elective coverage being capped at five times an employee’s salary sets the upper bound for any coverage, including what can be ported. This ensures that ported coverage does not exceed the original group limits established by the salary formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The salary-based cap on coverage informs the upper bound of what might be eligible for porting, influencing the scale of portable policies. Premiums for such ported policies are set using age-banded group rates regardless of the original coverage level.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The maximum coverage allowed under the plan is capped at five times an employee’s salary, defining the upper bound of potential benefits that could be converted or ported upon termination. This figure informs the scope of available protection during the transition period.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The maximum coverage being capped at five times an employee’s salary sets a financial ceiling that influences how much protection individuals might seek when transitioning out of the group plan. This limitation indirectly shapes the scope of what can be ported, though the conversion itself requires no proof of health.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">The $280,000 total coverage figure reflects a combination of basic and elective components, but its feasibility hinges on the employee earning enough to meet the fivefold salary threshold required for such elective amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a salary-linked ceiling on elective coverage, which directly constrains the feasibility of selecting $100,000 in voluntary coverage as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The $100,000 in supplemental coverage described in chunk_summary_1 must conform to the five-times-salary cap established in fact_sentence_2, meaning the employee’s salary determines whether such coverage is permissible.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
