      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="857a8b08-5757-46ee-b4bf-1c0a2ffd781c">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="72ff87e5-5a16-4d35-92e2-36614ac54990">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="40f620f4-6dba-4038-9a34-c3feaa1a6110">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">amount</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="767c68ae-b014-413e-ac0f-4059be5f4b3b">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="43215058-b03c-416f-8b02-f6b06ff4c8d9">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="086e155d-21a0-4017-a08f-067950973015">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends due to factors like job loss or policy termination—not due to unpaid premiums—the employee becomes eligible to convert to an individual policy. This condition arises directly from the termination criteria listed in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional trigger</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends due to termination of employment or other specified events, participants gain the option to convert to an individual whole life policy without providing evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage ends when employment stops or other triggering events occur, creating a deadline for participants to act. This termination event initiates the 31-day window during which individuals must submit a conversion application.</data>
      <data key="d4">termination leads to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">Termination of group coverage due to employment loss or other specified reasons enables access to conversion options. The converted individual policy is subject to standard premium rates applicable at that time.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">The termination of coverage under specified conditions enables participants to exercise their right to convert to an individual policy without undergoing a medical exam.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">Termination of coverage under specified conditions enables access to conversion options, where the maximum payout is capped at $200,000 regardless of prior group limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">Termination of coverage due to loss of eligibility or other specified reasons enables the employee to initiate conversion to an individual policy. This conversion process results in a new policy being issued based on the employee’s age at the moment of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">When an employee ceases active full-time employment—a condition listed in fact_sentence_1—they become eligible to port their group coverage into an individual policy, as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage ends upon specific triggering events such as loss of employment or premium non-payment. After termination, individuals may port their existing coverage amount into an individual policy without undergoing medical exams.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">Termination of employment triggers the end of group coverage, creating a deadline for action. This sets the context for fact_sentence_2, which establishes that individuals must act quickly—within 31 days—to secure continued protection through portability.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="9eb92b90-d878-4770-ab6d-789054602190">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage ends when employment stops or premiums lapse, triggering the opportunity to port coverage. After such termination, individuals must pay premiums directly to the insurer to maintain the converted policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">When coverage terminates due to loss of employment or other specified reasons, participants may elect to port their coverage. Premiums for such ported policies are determined by age-based group rates, ensuring continued affordability despite transition from group to individual plans.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">When employment ends, coverage terminates, triggering the right to port coverage. Since portability does not require evidence of insurability, individuals can transition to an individual policy easily after losing group coverage due to job loss.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers portability</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="25d2681b-ed64-4725-b142-ff262dcaee2c" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is triggered by</data>
    </edge>
