    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">Conversion rights apply when group coverage ends for reasons unrelated to premium default, ensuring continuity of life insurance access regardless of prior coverage limits set by salary.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional right</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">Conversion rights after termination rely on the existing benefit level established through annual recalculation, making prior adjustments relevant to the converted coverage amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert to an individual policy applies specifically when coverage ends through causes other than non-payment of premiums, such as resignation or termination of the master policy, as outlined in the list of triggering events.</data>
      <data key="d4">exempt from premium lapse</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends for reasons other than non-payment, employees qualify for conversion; this process is simplified by the absence of required health proofs.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends for reasons other than non-payment, the employee qualifies for conversion; the resulting individual policy is issued according to their current age at the time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions conversion</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">If group coverage ends for any reason except unpaid premiums, employees gain the right to convert to an individual policy. This right is contingent upon applying within 31 days after termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional precedence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends due to reasons other than unpaid premiums, employees gain the right to convert to an individual policy. This converted policy operates under standard premium rates applicable to such individual policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends due to reasons other than unpaid premiums, employees qualify to convert to an individual whole life policy, and this conversion does not require a medical examination.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends for reasons other than non-payment, employees qualify for conversion; however, the converted policy's maximum payout is limited by the lower of their previous group coverage or $200,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The right to convert coverage depends on timely action; if termination isn't due to unpaid premiums, employees have a limited period—within 31 days—to apply for conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends for reasons other than premium non-payment, employees may convert to an individual policy; the resulting ported coverage preserves the exact benefit level previously available under the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="9eb92b90-d878-4770-ab6d-789054602190">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert coverage after termination enables access to individual policies, whereupon premiums become payable directly to the insurance company instead of through the employer.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to an individual policy is permitted when group coverage ends for reasons other than unpaid premiums, and this process does not require proof of health or insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">When group coverage ends for reasons other than non-payment of premium, employees gain the right to convert to an individual policy; this converted coverage is subject to age-banded group rate pricing.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines conversion rights when group coverage ends for reasons other than premium default, enabling transition to an individual policy. Fact_sentence_2 extends this idea by allowing employees who leave employment to port their coverage into an individual policy, reinforcing continuity regardless of exit reason.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04" target="e84179b5-cb9a-4de7-95e8-6de7582de182">
      <data key="d3">The right to convert group coverage to an individual policy depends on being governed by California law, which establishes the regulatory environment under which such conversions are permitted.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="911a2af7-a822-45dc-a205-e57a399369e9" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers conversion privilege</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c224a58-7dfa-466e-8fbd-f7ad3e2efc49" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines termination date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="00761b5c-22ea-45ab-895c-b472670dcbdb" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is granted upon termination not due to non payment</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db930a94-a487-4091-9de0-c453b747ad52" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">defines timeframe for exercising conversion privilege</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="67497ca1-6858-4a35-b040-d0fe6a406d67" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is the resulting policy after conversion</data>
    </edge>
