    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="514bdb48-036d-415b-8666-eb466870949d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="0334304c-0079-42c9-9f8d-4a5b564f23f7">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The availability of conversion without proof of insurability applies specifically after coverage has terminated under one of the conditions outlined in the earlier statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to provide evidence of insurability is waived during conversion, enabling seamless access to individual policies after group coverage ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply within 31 days ensures participants can access the conversion privilege before it expires, making timely action necessary despite the absence of medical underwriting.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">Since no proof of insurability is required during conversion, the policy is issued promptly based on the employee’s actual age at the time of conversion, ensuring accurate premium calculation and benefit determination.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that conversion doesn't require proof of insurability, which aligns directly with fact sentence 2's claim that no medical exam is needed, reinforcing the ease of transition.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">Conversion allows individuals to obtain an individual policy without proving insurability, enabling them to enter a new contractual arrangement where standard premium rates apply.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a need for proof of insurability allows terminated employees to seamlessly transition their group coverage into an individual policy, facilitating the portability option upon job loss.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The lack of need for proof of insurability allows individuals to maintain their previous coverage amount when converting or porting policies, preserving financial protection after leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a medical exam requirement allows participants to convert coverage easily after leaving employment, while the maximum payout is limited to the lower of their previous group limit or $200,000, ensuring cost control for the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables limitation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that converting to an individual whole life policy avoids needing evidence of insurability. This aligns with fact sentence 2, which confirms that portability similarly waives such requirements, reinforcing a unified approach to accessibility after leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">similarity</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert coverage without proving insurability depends on timely action; applicants must submit their request within 31 days of employment cessation to qualify.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a medical exam requirement for conversion allows participants easy access to individual policies, enabling them to secure coverage at age-based group rates when porting benefits after leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without evidence of insurability, as stated in fact_sentence_2, enables the holder of the $280,000 coverage (from fact_sentence_1) to maintain protection post-employment regardless of health status.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without proof of insurability enables employees who opted for $100,000 in voluntary coverage to retain significant protection beyond employment, preserving their chosen benefit level.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables retention</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The availability of conversion to an individual whole life policy without medical evidence depends on the end of coverage, making the initial effective date of June 1, 2024, critical for determining eligibility timelines for such conversions.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that converting to an individual whole life policy avoids needing evidence of insurability, which directly supports the claim in fact_sentence_2 that portability similarly does not require such proof.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without proof of insurability supports long-term financial planning after employment loss, while the accelerated death benefit provides immediate liquidity for those facing terminal illness, offering complementary pathways for accessing funds under different life events.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without proof of insurability enables long-term protection continuity, which could indirectly support access to future accelerated benefits if a terminal diagnosis occurs later. However, the two facts concern different triggers and mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without proof of insurability supports access to long-term protection, while the option to accelerate part of the death benefit provides liquidity during terminal illness—both enabling flexibility in claim management under the same plan framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a medical exam requirement during conversion ensures access to individual policies post-employment, while the need for a certified death certificate later enables beneficiaries to collect benefits from those converted policies. These two facts support sequential steps in the lifecycle of coverage continuation and claim resolution.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The lack of insurability requirement for converting group coverage enables smoother access to long-term protection, ensuring beneficiaries can later file claims efficiently through designated channels like Alliance Group Benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables processing</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without evidence of insurability provides continuity of protection that could support long-term financial stability during periods of total disability, potentially enabling uninterrupted access to waived premiums through the disability clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="e84179b5-cb9a-4de7-95e8-6de7582de182">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual whole life policy without evidence of insurability operates under the legal framework established by California state law, ensuring enforceability and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca" target="be8734b0-e512-496b-b54a-fa04e79d616d">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without medical evidence supports continuity of coverage after employment loss, while the premium waiver provides financial relief during disability prior to age 65. These two provisions serve distinct but complementary roles in maintaining policyholder protection across transitions.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="75e11bc3-40e3-4423-928c-0bb7b204fd3d" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">enables conversion</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2dd2df14-4129-4e5a-85a9-aa7e751bd7ce" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">can be obtained without</data>
    </edge>
