    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">While the converted policy is issued at the employee’s attained age—which influences its cost—the overall amount covered cannot exceed the pre-established $1 million ceiling set by the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">The employee’s attained age at conversion influences the premium rate and terms of the new policy, which relies on the previously calculated benefit amount from the annual review.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="832e18bd-3db9-4b0d-a12a-09f2d351cc74">
      <data key="d3">An individual policy is issued at the employee’s attained age when converting from group coverage; this age factor interacts with the previously established salary-linked benefit levels during the transition.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The employee’s attained age at the time of conversion determines how the newly issued individual policy is priced and structured. Since conversion only applies after coverage has terminated under specific conditions outlined earlier, the timing of those terminations governs when the age-based determination takes place.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">An employee who converts group coverage after termination (excluding non-payment) receives an individual policy whose terms depend on their attained age at the moment of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">determines policy terms</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that the converted policy reflect the employee’s attained age ensures fair risk assessment despite the absence of medical underwriting, making the no-evidence-of-insurability rule feasible.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">The employee’s attained age at the time of conversion determines the premium rate and policy terms for the new individual policy. This condition applies only if the conversion request is made within the required 31-day window from termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">The employee's attained age at conversion sets the basis for determining applicable standard premium rates under the individual policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">determines</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">The policy's issuance at the employee’s attained age ensures accurate risk assessment upon conversion, which complements the lack of a medical exam by maintaining fairness despite omitted health screening.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">The employee’s attained age at conversion determines the pricing and issuance terms of the new policy, while the maximum payout is capped at either their prior group coverage level or $200,000, whichever is lower.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The converted policy is issued at the employee’s attained age when converting, ensuring accurate risk assessment based on current age. This reflects a critical aspect of the porting opportunity available upon employment termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The deadline for applying to port coverage depends on timely action after employment ends; however, it does not affect the determination of the insured's attained age used in issuing the new policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The employee’s attained age at conversion determines the applicable rate tier for premiums on ported coverage, ensuring pricing aligns with their current age category.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The policy being issued at the employee’s attained age depends on the lack of need for evidence of insurability, allowing seamless transition without health screening.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1111bb18-8dcf-4dd7-8088-221a8d35fca2" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">results in policy issuance at attained age</data>
    </edge>
