    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">Standard premium rates apply to the individual policy formed through conversion from group coverage, irrespective of the specific trigger for termination outlined in the prior statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">Standard premium rates apply to any individual whole life policy created through conversion from group coverage after termination not caused by premium default.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Standard premium rates govern the cost of the converted individual policy, meaning the absence of a medical exam (as stated in fact 1) leads directly to fixed rate-based pricing.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">Standard premium rates apply only when a conversion request is made within 31 days of termination, ensuring consistent pricing upon timely submission.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">Standard premium rates depend on the employee’s attained age at the time of conversion, ensuring accurate risk-based pricing.</data>
      <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for no medical exam ensures accessible entry into the individual policy, allowing participants to bypass health screening. Despite this relaxed underwriting, the policy applies standard premium rates, reflecting baseline risk assumptions used across the insurer’s portfolio.</data>
      <data key="d4">no medical requirement</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The converted policy's use of standard premium rates applies only after an employee leaves employment and chooses to convert their group coverage into an individual policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The ability to obtain a converted policy using standard premium rates depends on applying within 31 days after employment ends, making timely action essential for accessing the stated rate conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for standard premium rates applies regardless of health status, making it compatible with the absence of evidence of insurability during portability.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="95bbac19-7adf-44ba-b45f-a1f25b1ffd2a" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">uses standard premium rates</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="3f404929-5be6-4638-be22-fa546b81b890">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
