      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">amount</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="fcc15a7d-f95e-466a-a520-ef2f72982614">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="d9b55fe0-6d73-44c5-9536-6587a8d025b4">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="ca969513-62da-4cee-9ea9-e66f7342d5da">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">The $200,000 limit on conversion policies ensures that even if someone had higher group coverage, the post-conversion benefit cannot exceed this threshold, reinforcing the overall financial constraints established by the $1 million group cap.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">The $200,000 cap on conversion policies ensures that even if an employee had higher group coverage based on salary, the converted benefit cannot exceed this fixed threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">The conversion limit being capped at either the original group coverage or $200,000 means it is contingent upon the latest recalculated benefit amount established each year.</data>
      <data key="d4">sets limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="832e18bd-3db9-4b0d-a12a-09f2d351cc74">
      <data key="d3">The conversion limit of $200,000 or the previous group coverage amount constrains what can be achieved through salary-driven recalculations during active employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The $200,000 ceiling on conversion policies is contingent upon coverage having ended through any of the defined termination events outlined earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">The availability of conversion to an individual whole life policy upon termination (excluding non-payment) is subject to a cap of $200,000 or the original group limit, whichever is less.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Even though individuals can convert without proving insurability, the benefit amount is capped at $200,000 or their prior group coverage level, meaning the ease of conversion is balanced by a defined upper bound.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains access</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">To qualify for a conversion policy worth up to $200,000—or their previous group limit—an applicant must apply within 31 days after losing group coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">The maximum conversion benefit is limited to $200,000 or the previous group coverage, regardless of the employee’s age at conversion, though the actual cost of the policy reflects that age.</data>
      <data key="d4">sets cap</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The conversion benefit capped at $200,000 applies only when an employee has terminated employment and chooses to convert coverage, making the timing of departure essential for accessing this provision.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">The availability of a conversion policy capped at $200,000 or the prior group limit depends on being able to bypass medical underwriting, ensuring accessibility regardless of health status.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The maximum conversion benefit depends on timely application; failure to apply within 31 days disqualifies the participant from accessing even the capped $200,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">Conversion allows participants to switch to an individual policy with a maximum benefit capped at $200,000 or their prior group limit, whichever is lower. Ported coverage instead keeps the full amount from the group policy unchanged.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The maximum conversion benefit influences the scope of ported coverage, which in turn determines the applicable age-banded group rate for premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The conversion benefit is capped at $200,000 or the prior group limit, regardless of health status; meanwhile, portability allows continuation without evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">The limitation on conversion amounts ties into the ease of access enabled by waiving evidence of insurability, allowing eligible participants to secure coverage up to $200,000 without health screening.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The maximum conversion amount of $200,000 or prior group coverage could be diminished if any part of the death benefit is advanced before settlement, since such advances reduce the ultimate payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e">
      <data key="d3">The conversion limit described in fact_sentence_1 sets the upper bound for transferred coverage, which later determines the potential claimable amount. This ties indirectly to fact_sentence_2, where verifying beneficiary identity ensures correct disbursement of those converted benefits upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The conversion limit defined in fact_sentence_1 sets the upper bound for potential payouts from converted policies, which later triggers claims processing governed by fact_sentence_2's requirement to submit claims to the designated department.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9ebdd20f-93d7-4cdf-a918-5c33030b31b1" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c81634ba-c04a-48f6-b8d5-dc12183d9c6e" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b6cc109a-85f5-4901-8e75-e31f1bc04116" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is subject to limit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c40f60ee-60e0-4f33-a681-9cd4d10ba93c" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fcc15a7d-f95e-466a-a520-ef2f72982614" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9b55fe0-6d73-44c5-9536-6587a8d025b4" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is required within</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="49fb25c4-aa58-43ca-ac55-0dde03815d0a">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="bf320ebb-254b-48dd-a73c-c0ccb7c62b0b">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="5950199b-c06d-4adc-b893-17000409f9e3">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="0bcfaebf-fd0e-487e-82de-fd1992abd60e">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="3380983d-c6fe-450b-80b2-7ab43f18025f">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="c46812e5-3dc7-4269-b0c6-397b0401d8e1">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="b65433b3-085f-4623-aae5-a8db0ffb7407">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="9edf7983-077e-4cbb-b482-039aa880b4ee">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="c44b6e10-5e14-473b-923c-594bb4c5475d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="df959613-4c64-4b45-8a20-f798d5472d2a">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">amount</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="934b25b6-04fc-4282-a8dd-68234e7aac18">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="9a76b9f9-21b7-4ee8-a034-481eb42a2115">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="53a80153-9d4f-42bd-8678-6fd43a832a42">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The availability of conversion without a medical exam relies on prior termination of coverage, such as through loss of employment or policy lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a medical exam requirement enables seamless conversion to an individual whole life policy upon termination of group coverage for causes unrelated to premium default.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that no medical exam is required during conversion, supporting fact sentence 1’s assertion about not needing evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a medical exam makes it easier for individuals to complete the conversion process within the 31-day window specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a medical exam simplifies access to individual coverage, making it practical to issue policies at the employee’s current attained age without additional verification steps.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">Since no medical exam is required during conversion, individuals gain immediate access to an individual whole life policy regardless of health history. However, because the policy uses standard premium rates, the cost reflects average risk rather than personalized health data.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies standard rates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">The exemption from requiring a medical exam allows individuals to secure converted coverage, subject to the upper limit of either $200,000 or their previous group coverage level.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The lack of a medical exam requirement facilitates the ability of terminated employees to transfer their group coverage into an individual policy, making the transition smoother and more accessible.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The lack of a medical exam allows participants to seamlessly transfer their existing group coverage amount into an individual policy upon leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The lack of a medical exam requirement supports prompt action during the 31-day window, ensuring eligible individuals can secure coverage quickly upon leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to an individual policy allows participants to bypass medical exams, while ported coverage maintains affordability via age-based group rate tiers, ensuring continued access at predictable costs.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="9eb92b90-d878-4770-ab6d-789054602190">
      <data key="d3">Conversion to an individual policy requires no medical exam, enabling swift enrollment. After conversion, premium payments are made directly to the insurance company, ensuring continuity of coverage through personal responsibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that converting to an individual whole life policy requires no medical exam, which aligns with the broader principle stated in fact_sentence_2—that portability also does not require proof of insurability. Both provisions support seamless continuation of coverage post-employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 enables the conversion of the $280,000 group coverage outlined in fact_sentence_1 into an individual whole life policy without requiring a medical exam, preserving financial protection after employment ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables conversion</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The ability to convert group coverage to an individual policy without a medical exam enables retention of benefits like the $100,000 voluntary coverage upon leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences convertible benefit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The availability of a no-medical-exam conversion option applies specifically after the end of employment, meaning its applicability hinges on prior coverage beginning on June 1, 2024, thus grounding the conversion right in the initial effective date.</data>
      <data key="d4">enabled by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
