    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">An employee’s right to port coverage applies only to the amount of group coverage they held before termination, which is capped at $1 million.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4">
      <data key="d3">Upon leaving employment, individuals may transfer their existing group coverage to an individual policy. This option depends on any additional coverage previously elected, such as in $10,000 increments.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">Upon leaving employment, employees gain the ability to transfer their existing group coverage into an individual policy, regardless of health status, meaning the previously established salary-linked limits become the basis for the new individual coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">Upon leaving employment, individuals have the right to port their existing group coverage into an individual policy. This option depends on the previously established benefit level, which was determined through annual recalculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="832e18bd-3db9-4b0d-a12a-09f2d351cc74">
      <data key="d3">An employee who leaves employment may port their existing coverage, which was previously calculated according to their current salary.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The ability to port coverage upon leaving employment depends on the occurrence of that employment cessation, which is explicitly included as a termination trigger in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that departing employees can port their group coverage into an individual policy. This aligns with fact_sentence_1’s provision that allows conversion upon certain terminations, particularly those unrelated to premium lapses, suggesting overlapping pathways for maintaining life insurance protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Portability of coverage after employment cessation depends on being able to convert without medical underwriting, making the lack of insurability requirements essential to its implementation.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">Employees who terminate employment gain the right to port coverage; however, this benefit is only available if applied for within 31 days of departure.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">Employees who leave employment may port their group coverage into an individual policy without medical exams, subject to timing and limits; this process relies on being issued at their attained age at conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">An employee who leaves employment becomes eligible to convert their group coverage into an individual policy, which then operates under standard premium rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">An employee who leaves employment gains the right to convert or port coverage, enabling them to access the $200,000 cap on individual policies through either method.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">Employees who leave their jobs can port their coverage to an individual policy, made possible because no medical examination is required during the process.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">An employee who leaves employment has the option to port their group coverage into an individual policy, but only if they apply within 31 days after leaving.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">When an employee leaves employment, they have the option to port their group coverage into an individual policy. This ported coverage preserves the exact benefit level previously available under the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">ports to retain</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">An employee leaving employment gains the right to port their group coverage; once ported, the new individual policy operates under age-based group premium rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="9eb92b90-d878-4770-ab6d-789054602190">
      <data key="d3">An employee who leaves employment may port their group coverage into an individual policy; once ported, they become responsible for paying premiums directly to the insurance company.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">An employee who leaves employment may port their group coverage to an individual policy, and this process does not require providing evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">The right to port coverage after leaving employment enables the preservation of the $280,000 group coverage as an individual policy, subject to applicable limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables porting</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 enables continuation of the $100,000 voluntary coverage outlined in fact_sentence_1 through conversion or porting options after job termination, preserving access beyond active employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables porting</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The right to port coverage after leaving employment implies that the initial effective date of June 1, 2024, marks the beginning of the period from which such transition rights become available, assuming no earlier lapses.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
