    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="24579823-b08f-45f4-952c-10c5f85a539f">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">The retained coverage amount during porting is subject to the $1 million maximum, meaning the actual transferred benefit cannot surpass this threshold regardless of previous levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4">
      <data key="d3">The retained amount during porting depends on the level of coverage selected earlier through incremental elections, meaning higher elected amounts result in greater potential ported limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">determined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">Ported coverage retains the exact amount from the group policy, meaning it is directly constrained by the initial salary-linked ceiling described in the first sentence, ensuring consistency across transitions.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">The retained amount from the group policy during porting depends entirely on the most recently calculated benefit, which is set through annual recalculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="832e18bd-3db9-4b0d-a12a-09f2d351cc74">
      <data key="d3">Coverage ported to an individual policy preserves the exact benefit level previously established under the group plan, which itself relies on the employee’s current salary at time of recalculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The ability to port coverage at the same level as the prior group policy relies on the occurrence of a terminating event defined in the initial clause, ensuring continuity of benefit levels post-termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">The preservation of the prior group coverage amount during porting depends on qualifying for conversion after termination not caused by premium default, ensuring consistent protection post-transition.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Maintaining the same coverage amount upon porting ensures that beneficiaries retain the intended death benefit, which is only possible because no medical underwriting is required during the process.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">Maintaining the pre-existing coverage amount upon transfer relies on submitting the application within 31 days of leaving the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">Ported coverage mirrors the pre-existing group coverage amount exactly, maintaining continuity. In contrast, converted policies are limited by a fixed upper bound of $200,000 regardless of past levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">Maintaining the same coverage amount ensures that individuals who avoid a medical exam still retain full financial protection equivalent to their previous group policy limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The ability to port coverage after leaving employment depends on maintaining the same coverage amount from the group policy, ensuring continuity of benefit levels during transition.</data>
      <data key="d4">retains amount</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The ability to maintain original coverage amounts upon porting depends on applying within the specified timeframe after employment ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The amount of coverage remains unchanged when transitioning from group to individual through porting, and premiums for this maintained coverage are set using age-banded group rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">maintains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="9eb92b90-d878-4770-ab6d-789054602190">
      <data key="d3">The ported coverage preserves the prior group policy's benefit amount, necessitating direct premium payments to the insurance company to sustain the continued coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">maintains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The retention of the original group coverage amount during portability depends on the lack of need for evidence of insurability, ensuring seamless transition without underwriting barriers.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">Coverage portability ensures that the $280,000 benefit level maintained under the group policy continues into an individual policy without requiring new underwriting.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The rule allowing ported coverage to maintain its previous amount supports the validity of retaining the $100,000 voluntary addition established under the original group policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">Coverage portability preserves the existing benefit amount established on June 1, 2024, ensuring continuity of benefits after departure from the group plan, assuming timely action within the 31-day window.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577">
      <data key="d3">Ported coverage preserves pre-existing limits post-employment, whereas disability-based premium waivers allow ongoing coverage without payment due to incapacity; these apply under different triggers and are mutually exclusive scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a">
      <data key="d3">Porting coverage preserves prior benefits after leaving employment, while the premium waiver allows uninterrupted coverage during prolonged disability—both enabling sustained protection under different circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47">
      <data key="d3">Porting coverage preserves prior benefits after leaving employment, while the premium waiver allows continued coverage without paying premiums if disabled before age 60. These mechanisms serve distinct purposes—one enables retention of coverage after job loss, the other ensures affordability during long-term disability.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9" target="e84179b5-cb9a-4de7-95e8-6de7582de182">
      <data key="d3">The ability to port coverage at the same level depends on being governed by California law, which establishes the legal foundation for such transition rights.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad2ae21a-ba68-47f3-a632-23599df132de" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is preserved</data>
    </edge>
