    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply within 31 days of termination enables timely access to portability options, including those subject to the $1 million coverage cap, ensuring continuity of protection under defined limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">time dependent on cap</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">An employee has only 31 days from the end of employment to apply for portability, ensuring timely action before losing access to guaranteed coverage options; this deadline applies regardless of the specific coverage level determined by salary-based calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply for portability within 31 days hinges on the occurrence of employment termination, one of the key reasons covered by fact_sentence_1 for losing group coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">A 31-day deadline applies specifically to conversions triggered by non-premium-related terminations, ensuring that eligible individuals act promptly to secure new coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">time dependent</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">To take advantage of the no-medical-exam conversion privilege, individuals must act quickly by applying within 31 days of losing their job.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">The need to act within 31 days of terminating employment applies equally to both conversion and portability rights. Since conversion depends on the loss of group coverage—which coincides with job termination—this timeline ensures participants retain flexibility regardless of whether they choose conversion or portability.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">The date of conversion determines the employee’s attained age, which sets the basis for issuing the new policy, regardless of when the application was submitted—as long as it meets the 31-day window.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">Applying within 31 days of termination ensures eligibility to secure a converted policy with standard premium rates, fulfilling the key precondition for that benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">Applying within 31 days ensures eligibility for the maximum conversion benefit, which cannot exceed $200,000 or the prior group limit.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">Timely application within 31 days ensures access to favorable conversion terms, including exemption from medical exams.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply within 31 days of termination ensures that employees retain access to portability options when transitioning from group to individual coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">Applying within 31 days ensures participants retain their prior group coverage limits when converting to an individual policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="9eb92b90-d878-4770-ab6d-789054602190">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply within 31 days of termination ensures that individuals qualify for portability, enabling them to begin paying premiums directly to the insurer for continued coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that portability applications occur within 31 days of employment termination ensures timely enrollment into the ported policy, enabling participants to secure coverage at age-banded group rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply within 31 days of termination is meaningful because it allows individuals to act before losing access to favorable conversion terms, such as no need for evidence of insurability.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply for portability within 31 days of termination, as stated in fact_sentence_2, enables the preservation of the $280,000 group coverage amount outlined in fact_sentence_1 through conversion to an individual policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply for portability within 31 days of termination enables the continuation of coverage equivalent to prior levels—including the $100,000 voluntary component—ensuring no loss of benefits due to timing.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day window for portability applications depends on the end of employment, but its feasibility hinges on having accurate records of the original coverage effective date, such as June 1, 2024, from fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply within 31 days aligns with the absence of evidence of insurability, ensuring timely access to portable coverage without health-related hurdles.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">Portability rights allow terminated employees to maintain coverage up to $200,000 within 31 days, while the $250,000 cap applies specifically to accelerated benefits for terminally ill individuals, representing a distinct mechanism for accessing funds before death.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply for portability within 31 days of leaving employment creates urgency around accessing benefits, including potential use of accelerated death benefits which lower the ultimate payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day deadline for portability ensures continued access to life insurance benefits after job loss, enabling beneficiaries to maintain coverage. This step precedes potential future claims, where a certified death certificate becomes necessary to validate entitlement and trigger payouts.</data>
      <data key="d4">sequential dependence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="0fb61d44-5bc9-4a23-945d-cec5a551fb86">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day deadline for portability ensures timely access to individual coverage options after leaving employment, which enables beneficiaries to file claims later; however, it does not affect the speed of payment once a claim is filed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to apply for portability within 31 days of termination may intersect with the premium waiver period—if an employee leaves due to disability and later returns to work, their ability to act on portability depends on timely action despite extended absence from employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d" target="e84179b5-cb9a-4de7-95e8-6de7582de182">
      <data key="d3">The 31-day window for portability applications is a key procedural detail within the broader scope of the life insurance policy, which operates under California law. While the legal jurisdiction doesn't affect the timeline itself, it establishes the regulatory environment governing such provisions.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
