    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates apply to ported coverage, ensuring consistent pricing; however, these rates are constrained by the overall $1 million ceiling on total coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="99e61209-41c5-4149-bde4-f456557bdca4">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates apply to any ported coverage, including that resulting from electing additional $10,000 increments during participation.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates apply to any ported coverage, meaning that even though coverage is capped at five times salary, the cost reflects group pricing by age rather than individual risk assessment.</data>
      <data key="d4">determined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates apply to ported coverage regardless of prior benefit levels, meaning that even though benefits are recalculated annually, the premium rate depends solely on the participant’s age at time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="832e18bd-3db9-4b0d-a12a-09f2d351cc74">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates applied to ported coverage depend on the insured's age at time of conversion, reflecting the prior benefit level determined by salary-based recalculations, thus aligning premium costs with previously established coverage limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The availability of age-banded group rates for ported coverage presupposes that coverage has terminated under one of the conditions listed, such as cessation of employment or non-payment of premiums, enabling conversion rights.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">The availability of age-banded group rates for ported coverage depends on the prior condition being met—that group coverage terminated for reasons other than non-payment of premium, allowing conversion rights.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates apply to ported coverage, ensuring predictable costs; however, this benefit is only available because conversion does not require proof of insurability, allowing seamless continuation regardless of health changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates for ported coverage are contingent upon submitting an application within 31 days of termination, making timeliness essential for accessing this pricing tier.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">Ported coverage uses age-banded group rates, meaning the premium amount is set according to the employee’s age at the time of conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">determines</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">Age-based pricing for ported coverage relies on the insured’s prior group limit, capping at $200,000, thus linking back to the conversion benefit ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates apply to ported policies, enabling affordable continuation; importantly, such transitions occur without requiring a medical examination.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The availability of ported coverage depends on timely action after job loss, and the resulting individual policy uses age-banded group rates rather than standard individual pricing.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">Since ported coverage preserves the original group policy's benefit amount, its pricing uses age-banded group rates rather than standard individual underwriting rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">determines</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">Age-banded group rates apply only to those who successfully apply for ported coverage within the 31-day window post-termination, making the deadline essential for accessing this pricing tier.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d" target="9eb92b90-d878-4770-ab6d-789054602190">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains that ported coverage uses age-based group rates, defining how much the premium amounts are calculated. Fact sentence 2 states that those premiums must be paid directly to the insurance company, clarifying where payments go.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
