    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="3721319d-49fa-40bf-858f-e5fff2b66d74">
      <data key="d3">Portability allows individuals to transition to an individual policy without proving insurability, enabling timely continuation of coverage; however, the amount transferred is limited by existing group coverage caps such as the $1 million ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual constraint</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="9690cd42-7774-4809-a8ce-a06325472dfc">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that no evidence of insurability is needed during portability ensures accessibility to converted policies regardless of health changes since enrollment. While unrelated to salary calculations, this provision supports equitable access to continued coverage, complementing the initial benefit design defined by salary-linked caps.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="ea3ec25d-9582-4df4-a238-3ee4af975a34">
      <data key="d3">Portability allows participants to transfer group coverage to an individual policy without providing evidence of insurability upon job loss. This feature relies on prior benefit calculations being accurate and up-to-date, ensuring eligible individuals retain meaningful coverage limits when transitioning out of the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="87cd45fe-5845-4daf-8291-66684bb077e9">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a requirement for evidence of insurability enables seamless portability after coverage ends, particularly upon termination of employment, ensuring access to continued protection regardless of health changes since joining the group plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables transition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="61937f46-373a-4006-9ace-d654c1af6a04">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a requirement for evidence of insurability enables employees to smoothly transition from group to individual coverage after leaving employment, even if the reason was not related to missed payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 notes that portability doesn't require evidence of insurability, mirroring fact sentence 1’s assertion about conversion being available without proof of health, suggesting equivalent treatment for both pathways.</data>
      <data key="d4">similarity</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a need for evidence of insurability allows participants to complete the portability process swiftly after termination, making it feasible to meet the 31-day deadline specified in the prior statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="cb39d508-63bc-4d1f-b31d-8e17c8da36fc">
      <data key="d3">The waiver of evidence of insurability ensures that employees can have policies issued at their attained age upon conversion, regardless of health status.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="aa55d164-41ad-4557-9ee0-9d585db80f12">
      <data key="d3">Since no evidence of insurability is needed for portability, individuals can transition to an individual policy at standard rates without undergoing medical evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">Portability does not require proof of insurability, enabling access to converted coverage that remains subject to a $200,000 or previous limit ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="4ec56b43-419b-48f6-9329-06f8c3d46b41">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that portability allows individuals to transfer coverage without providing evidence of insurability, reinforcing the same relaxed underwriting condition described in fact_sentence_1 regarding conversion to an individual policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="a9f431d0-a3a3-4a6f-a8b7-104c24124f59">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a requirement for evidence of insurability enables employees to successfully port their coverage after leaving employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">Without requiring evidence of insurability, individuals can successfully port their existing coverage amount to an individual policy, preserving their prior benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The lack of requirement for evidence of insurability enables timely applications within the 31-day window, ensuring accessibility regardless of health changes post-employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="d986ae35-896f-42e2-ade3-c28663178d9d">
      <data key="d3">The absence of evidence of insurability allows for streamlined access to ported coverage at favorable age-banded group rates.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="a2314015-ba2f-446d-8508-e444ccc759b1">
      <data key="d3">The absence of evidence-of-insurability requirements enables employees to retain or transfer coverage beyond employment; since the original coverage was $280,000, this figure defines the baseline for potential converted or portable benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="9fa5fe2f-bcde-4972-ab81-4ae967ccf64b">
      <data key="d3">The provision allowing portability without evidence of insurability supports the continuation of the $100,000 voluntary coverage originally selected by the employee, ensuring access even after job loss.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on coverage</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The absence of evidence-of-insurability requirements for portability allows employees who lose coverage due to job loss to maintain protection even after leaving the company, regardless of health status—this complements the fixed effective date by ensuring continuity of risk management beyond the original coverage period.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that portability does not require evidence of insurability, which aligns exactly with fact sentence 2. Both statements are reinforced by their respective chunk summaries describing non-medical requirements during conversion or transfer of coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">The absence of insurability requirements for portability enables beneficiaries to maintain coverage after job loss, which could support financial stability during prolonged illnesses like those qualifying for accelerated death benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The ability to port coverage without proving insurability ensures continued protection after leaving employment, but any early withdrawal of funds diminishes the eventual death benefit available to beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">Portability allows terminated employees to retain coverage without proving health, while the accelerated benefit reduces future payments through an actuarial discount—both enabling flexible claims handling but at different stages.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">Portability allows terminated employees to retain coverage without proving insurability, which complements the provision enabling accelerations of up to $250,000 by removing health-based barriers to accessing funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">The absence of insurability requirements for portability enables beneficiaries to maintain coverage after job loss, facilitating smoother access to future claims—but filing a claim still requires formal documentation like a certified death certificate.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The absence of insurability requirements for portability enables smoother transitions into individual policies, but successful implementation depends on timely submission of claims through the designated department.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47">
      <data key="d3">The ability to port coverage without proving insurability complements the premium waiver feature by ensuring continuous protection under distinct circumstances—job loss versus disability—but does not rely on it.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577">
      <data key="d3">The absence of insurability requirement for portability complements the premium waiver feature by ensuring continuous access to coverage under adverse circumstances, such as leaving employment or becoming disabled, without additional health scrutiny.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87" target="e84179b5-cb9a-4de7-95e8-6de7582de182">
      <data key="d3">The absence of insurability requirements for portability aligns with standard provisions often codified in state-specific regulations like those in California, where such policies operate.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual support</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="74be7580-041c-4295-a676-6fc4073e4368" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is subject to portability without requiring evidence of insurability</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ed77f15d-5502-467f-9b75-6dc9c24bec77" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">defines eligibility cutoff date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="61a1c444-2b80-4e68-a7dc-a9724f1a734b" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is exercisable without medical proof</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9a4b342d-c990-44f1-b933-f568fa9b20bd" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">timeframe for exercise of portability</data>
