    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">The presence of group coverage enables the provision of portable benefits, allowing members to retain coverage without additional underwriting requirements during transfers.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage enables access to special provisions like the accelerated death benefit for terminally ill individuals.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">The presence of group coverage enables the provision of special benefits like accelerated death benefits for terminally ill individuals.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage is offered by the insurer, creating the framework under which benefit accelerations like the $5,000 minimum may apply. This foundational context enables understanding of how advances work within the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage enables access to specific benefits like accelerated death benefits, establishing the context in which the $250,000 limit operates.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage enables access to benefits such as accelerated death benefits, which are subject to an actuarial discount to reflect the early payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The group life insurance plan offered by the insurer enables access to partial death benefits, which results in a reduced final payout to beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="50012b48-7eab-42a1-9339-4f987a82053c">
      <data key="d3">The group coverage offered by the insurance company includes the absence of limitations based on pre-existing medical conditions, enhancing accessibility for applicants.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="72af3f2b-1c51-48ee-8da5-c36c14e9735e">
      <data key="d3">The existence of group coverage enables the application of specific exclusions like the one regarding suicide within the first year. Without the foundational framework of group insurance, such clauses would lack operational context.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7">
      <data key="d3">The presence of group coverage enables administrative functions such as updating beneficiaries through HR. This operational capability relies on the underlying group plan being active.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="6158d9a5-ff94-4835-99aa-58729bb45911">
      <data key="d3">The group life insurance plan offered by the insurer includes provisions for distributing benefits among multiple beneficiaries, ensuring equitable division unless otherwise directed.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="80ef03d9-a0d8-4e34-b854-917b328e532c">
      <data key="d3">Group coverage enables the administration of benefits through designated channels, allowing for alternative disbursement paths such as paying the estate when no living beneficiaries remain.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="afec02f1-3018-4d35-a72f-90bd5e82289f">
      <data key="d3">The insurance company providing group coverage necessitates beneficiary notification to initiate claims processing. Without the insurer’s role, such notifications would have no purpose or recipient.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">Since the insurance company provides the group coverage, it follows that they would also make the claim form accessible to policyholders, ensuring smooth claims processing.</data>
      <data key="d4">supplies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace">
      <data key="d3">The presence of group coverage by an insurance company necessitates formal procedures like submitting a claim form to access benefits, establishing a foundational link between policy provision and claims processing.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The insurance company providing group coverage implies responsibility for handling claims through its designated department, making it necessary to direct submissions to Alliance Group Benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies department</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">The presence of group coverage by an insurance company enables the formal claims process, during which a certified death certificate is required as part of the submission requirements.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d" target="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e">
      <data key="d3">The existence of group coverage enables the claims process, under which verifying beneficiary identity becomes a required step. Without active coverage, claims would not be processed, making identity validation irrelevant.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
