    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">Portability without evidence of insurability relies on the underlying framework of group coverage established by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">The ability to transfer coverage without evidence of insurability enables smoother access to benefits like the accelerated death benefit, especially important for those facing serious illnesses who may need timely financial support.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">Fact 1 states that individuals can transfer their coverage without proving insurability, enabling continuity of protection. Fact 2 explains that those with a terminal diagnosis can access up to 75% of their death benefit early, subject to actuarial adjustment.</data>
      <data key="d4">portability supports acceleration</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">Portability eliminates the need for evidence of insurability, facilitating access to benefits such as accelerated payments. However, each acceleration directly diminishes the total death benefit available to beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">Portability without requiring proof of insurability ensures continuity of coverage, enabling eligible individuals to potentially access accelerated benefits such as the maximum $250,000 payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">Portability eliminates the need for proof of insurability, allowing beneficiaries or policyholders to transfer coverage easily. This facilitates early access to funds through accelerated benefits, which are subsequently reduced by an actuarial discount to reflect the earlier payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms that portability doesn't require evidence of insurability, aligning with fact_sentence_1’s assertion about conversion being possible without medical evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="8eab46db-8762-4987-ab49-5c7a33da05bf">
      <data key="d3">Portability without evidence of insurability enables eligible individuals to meet the 31-day deadline for conversion, ensuring uninterrupted protection despite potential health changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">The lack of need for proof of insurability facilitates the ability to convert to an individual policy with a maximum benefit capped at either $200,000 or prior group coverage, ensuring accessible transition options post-employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 reiterates that no evidence of insurability is needed for portability, matching the content of fact sentence 1. This repetition is substantiated in both chunk summaries, confirming consistent messaging regarding access to individual policies post-termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">1.0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">The lack of need for proof of insurability supports the urgency implied by the 31-day window, making it easier for terminated employees to secure continued protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances timeliness</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The absence of evidence-of-insurability requirement for portability ensures that employees like those covered under the master policy can maintain protection seamlessly after leaving employment, validating the significance of such certificates.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">Portability without requiring evidence of insurability relies on the existence of a formal Master Group Policy administered through the employer, making it foundational to such flexible transition terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">Portability allowing coverage transfer without evidence of insurability operates within the broader contractual boundaries defined by the master policy's terms, ensuring continuity despite changing circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d4">suppords</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">Portability provisions ensure uninterrupted coverage continuity, supporting the validity of Jordan Casey Taylor’s role as spouse beneficiary should the insured leave employment and maintain coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
