    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">The availability of an accelerated death benefit requires prior establishment of group coverage by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">Qualifying for an accelerated death benefit due to terminal illness underscores the importance of flexible portability rules, ensuring beneficiaries can maintain coverage even after significant health changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement of a terminal illness diagnosis with a life expectancy of 12 months or less enables qualification for accelerating up to 75% of the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
      <data key="d3">Individuals diagnosed with a terminal illness and having a life expectancy of 12 months or less may access an accelerated death benefit, with a minimum payout set at $5,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">An individual diagnosed with a terminal illness and having a life expectancy of 12 months or less may access an accelerated death benefit, capped at $250,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">caps</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">If a policyholder has a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, they may access part of their death benefit early. However, each dollar taken reduces the total amount available to beneficiaries upon death.</data>
      <data key="d4">qualifies for reduction</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">If a policyholder has a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, they qualify for an accelerated death benefit. However, the actual amount received will be lowered due to an actuarial discount applied to account for early payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace">
      <data key="d3">If someone has a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, they may access part of their death benefit early. To do so, they must submit a completed claim form along with other required documents.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">An individual diagnosed with a terminal illness and meeting the life expectancy requirement may qualify for an accelerated death benefit. To initiate such a claim, the necessary paperwork—including the claim form—is accessible through either the employer or the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">If someone has a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less, they may qualify for an accelerated death benefit, which requires submitting a claim to the designated department.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e">
      <data key="d3">The ability to access an accelerated death benefit upon terminal illness diagnosis requires subsequent submission of documents, including verification of beneficiary identity, to initiate the claim process.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">The accelerated death benefit provision applies before death, allowing terminally ill policyholders to access funds early. In contrast, submitting a certified death certificate is part of the formal claim process that occurs only after the insured's passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">posterior to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="48d672b8-4057-4fee-8100-1e2361e1ca93">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines who qualifies for an early payout based on medical status, while fact_sentence_2 gives the phone number to contact for initiating such a claim. The second fact supports the practical next step after qualifying under the first.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="22c4b994-6a5b-49d5-a129-731be848f272">
      <data key="d3">An individual diagnosed with a terminal illness and meeting the life expectancy criterion may initiate a claim for an accelerated death benefit, leading to a timely resolution after submitting necessary documentation.</data>
      <data key="d4">eligibility leads to claim processing</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Access to accelerated death benefits enables terminally ill individuals to draw partial payouts before death, which could influence decisions about converting group coverage into an individual policy, especially if future premium payments become unaffordable.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">Accelerated death benefits provide immediate liquidity for terminally ill individuals, potentially reducing reliance on future portability options by addressing urgent needs earlier in the process.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances access</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4eab017e-b004-4c26-b115-76339b6fa6b5" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is qualified by</data>
    </edge>
