    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="4a16511c-dfa0-4277-96a1-d7cef5fdd8a8">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">document</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="8faca5fd-5e2f-4586-9b42-305525069bf3">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="c8a90c1f-3505-4cc8-aca0-3e6e0e8ae501">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">The availability of accelerated death benefits requires that group coverage exists through the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">Fact 2 outlines the option to accelerate part of the death benefit upon a terminal illness diagnosis. Fact 1 ensures that such accelerated benefits remain accessible even during transfers of coverage, preserving rights across transitions.</data>
      <data key="d4">acceleration compliments portability</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">Receiving up to 75% of the death benefit through acceleration requires being diagnosed with a terminal illness and having a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the cap at 75% of the death benefit for early payouts due to terminal illness, while fact_sentence_2 ensures that even the smallest allowable advance meets a minimum threshold of $5,000, establishing a practical lower boundary for eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">sets limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the eligibility criterion for benefit acceleration based on terminal illness diagnosis, while fact_sentence_2 sets the absolute ceiling ($250,000) on how much can be accessed under that provision.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">If an individual accelerates part of their death benefit due to a terminal illness, the total amount available to beneficiaries after death will be reduced by the amount already received.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">If an individual requests early access to part of their death benefit due to a terminal illness, the amount they receive will be lower than the nominal 75% because of an actuarial adjustment designed to reflect the earlier disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace">
      <data key="d3">The ability to accelerate benefits upon terminal diagnosis requires submission of standard claim documentation, such as a completed claim form, ensuring procedural compliance during the process.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">A terminally ill individual can access up to 75% of their death benefit through an acceleration process requiring a claim form. This form is accessible through either the employer or the insurer, enabling the beneficiary to initiate the request.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The ability to accelerate benefits due to a terminal illness requires submitting a claim to the designated department, ensuring proper processing and verification.</data>
      <data key="d4">procedural requirement</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="a4660611-ebc8-4a98-ae71-7b04c1befa54">
      <data key="d3">Requesting an accelerated death benefit requires submitting claim forms, which must be sent to a specific address. The mailing address serves as part of the administrative pathway for processing such requests.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="22c4b994-6a5b-49d5-a129-731be848f272">
      <data key="d3">The ability to accelerate up to 75% of the death benefit upon terminal diagnosis initiates the claims process, leading to payment within ten business days once all required documents are received.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Receiving an accelerated death benefit due to a terminal illness depends on active coverage at time of diagnosis, which relies on maintaining enrollment through employment or timely conversion to an individual policy—such as allowed by the non-medical conversion provision described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The availability of accelerating up to 75% of the death benefit supports the practical application of the coverage confirmed by the certificate, enhancing its real-world significance.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">The ability to accelerate up to 75% of the death benefit depends on being enrolled under a qualifying group policy, such as the one administered through the employer as stated in the master agreement.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on policy</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a benefit feature—accelerated death benefits—that operates under the authority established by fact_sentence_1, where the Master Policy governs interpretive conflicts.</data>
      <data key="d4">subordinate to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies a particular exception to standard payout rules—accelerated benefits—which is consistent with but further defines the general contractual framework described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">If the insured exercises the option to accelerate up to 75% of the death benefit due to a terminal illness, the resulting lower payout may alter the financial outcome for the primary beneficiary, Jordan Casey Taylor, who was originally set to receive the full $280,000.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">If the insured receives an accelerated benefit due to a terminal illness, it would reduce the eventual death benefit payable to Jordan Casey Taylor, who is listed as the primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">A terminal illness claim enabling up to 75% acceleration of the death benefit directly affects the ultimate payout to the primary beneficiary, who would normally receive 100%, thus modifying the outcome described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="52b0c634-376a-4bbe-a0e1-f374e691f95a">
      <data key="d3">If a terminal illness triggers an advance of up to 75% of the death benefit, it reduces the ultimate payout available to the Taylor Family Revocable Trust as the contingent beneficiary, altering its potential inheritance.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects beneficiary</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a" target="0fd4ce41-df87-49ef-b846-edcb6c8e3ffc">
      <data key="d3">If the insured uses the terminal illness acceleration feature, the eventual payout to the contingent beneficiary would be less than 100%, since prior advances reduce the available benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces payout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0f3bf776-1ee7-4d6f-862e-881210e7b3f2" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">provides</data>
    </edge>
