    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="d362aa56-9922-4db9-bd41-481e6b96ae74">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="045e9659-a332-446a-8ebb-a41061d1e575">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">The $5,000 minimum acceleration amount applies specifically within the scope of the group life insurance plan already established by the provider, making it contingent on prior coverage setup.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">The availability of a minimum accelerated benefit of $5,000 depends on qualifying under the terminal illness provision, requiring a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables minimum</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 defines the minimum acceleration amount at $5,000, it only applies meaningfully in context with fact_sentence_1, which permits such advances under specific conditions like terminal illness diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d4">enforces floor</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">The minimum acceleration amount is set at $5,000, but any such advance is subject to an actuarial discount that reduces its value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the minimum threshold at $5,000 for early access to benefits, establishing the lowest allowable advance. Fact_sentence_2 specifies the cap at $250,000, defining the highest amount available under the same provision.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The minimum acceleration amount is set at $5,000, meaning any withdrawal cannot be less than this figure. This ensures that even small advances have measurable impact on reducing the ultimate death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace">
      <data key="d3">The minimum acceleration amount of $5,000 establishes a baseline for early payouts, while submitting a completed claim form is a mandatory step in triggering such payments. These elements together define key parameters of the claims procedure.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">The minimum acceleration amount sets a baseline for eligible requests, enabling beneficiaries to access funds early under specific conditions. This requirement informs who may initiate a claim, making the availability of the claim form relevant to those meeting the threshold.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="afec02f1-3018-4d35-a72f-90bd5e82289f">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the floor for early benefit payouts, ensuring recipients get at least $5,000. This financial detail informs beneficiaries about potential relief, motivating prompt action like contacting Alliance Group Benefits after the insured's passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The minimum acceleration amount of $5,000 sets a threshold for early payouts, while claims involving such advances must be formally submitted to the designated department at Alliance Group Benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">procedural dependence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The $5,000 minimum acceleration limit applies to insured individuals covered under the Master Group Policy, consistent with the coverage details provided in the certificate.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a $5,000 minimum acceleration limit implies practical constraints on benefit distribution under the Master Group Policy managed by the employer.</data>
      <data key="d4">has condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88">
      <data key="d3">The $5,000 minimum acceleration provision operates within the scope defined by higher-level policies such as the Master Policy, whose authority supersedes this certificate in case of inconsistency.</data>
      <data key="d4">subordinate to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a $5,000 minimum acceleration amount depends on the overarching policy rules governing coverage, such as those defined in the Master Policy referenced in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">subordinate to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">The designation of Jordan Casey Taylor as primary beneficiary means they would be entitled to receive any accelerated benefit payments, provided eligibility criteria such as the $5,000 minimum are met.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">The $5,000 minimum acceleration provision applies to eligible beneficiaries like Jordan Casey Taylor, who is designated as the primary beneficiary under the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to beneficiary</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">While the $5,000 minimum acceleration applies only in cases of terminal illness, it directly impacts the eventual payout—the same payout referenced in the statement that the primary beneficiary receives 100%, meaning accelerations reduce what remains for heirs.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects final payout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a" target="0fd4ce41-df87-49ef-b846-edcb6c8e3ffc">
      <data key="d3">While the contingent beneficiary inherits the entire benefit upon the insured’s death, the ability to accelerate part of the benefit (minimum $5,000) reduces the ultimate amount payable to them, potentially impacting their inheritance.</data>
      <data key="d4">affected by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a0f4356c-02d0-4503-82d7-3b7849614d39" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
