    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 ceiling on accelerated payments only applies within the framework of group life insurance coverage offered by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a $250,000 ceiling on accelerated payments underscores the financial parameters governing how much can be accessed, even when portability eliminates the need for new underwriting.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 ceiling applies specifically to those qualifying due to a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines the maximum dollar amount available for early payout due to terminal illness, which directly applies to and limits the scope of what is allowed by fact_sentence_1’s 75% rule.</data>
      <data key="d4">constrains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the maximum acceleration limit of $250,000, providing context for how much can be accessed upfront. This complements fact_sentence_1 by setting the upper boundary of the financial range defined by the policy's accelerated benefit feature.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222">
      <data key="d3">The maximum acceleration cap of $250,000 is subject to adjustment through an actuarial discount, meaning the actual amount paid out will be less than the nominal maximum.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The maximum acceleration cap of $250,000 sets the upper bound for early payouts, but any such withdrawal diminishes the remaining death benefit available to beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="afec02f1-3018-4d35-a72f-90bd5e82289f">
      <data key="d3">The maximum acceleration amount sets a financial ceiling for early payouts, which informs the scope of benefits available during the claims process initiated by beneficiary notification.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">The maximum acceleration amount sets a cap on benefits, while the availability of the claim form ensures applicants can initiate the process. Both contribute to understanding how beneficiaries access funds under the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual relation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the maximum acceleration available from the death benefit, which sets a boundary for potential payouts. Fact_sentence_2 identifies a necessary step in accessing those benefits by specifying documentation needs.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The ability to accelerate up to $250,000 aligns with the broader framework allowing non-medical transitions like portability, reinforcing accessibility regardless of current health status.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">While the $250,000 acceleration limit pertains only to terminally ill beneficiaries seeking early payouts, the 31-day rule ensures timely conversion or porting of group coverage into individual policies upon job loss, regardless of health status.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 maximum acceleration threshold applies specifically to policies like the one referenced in the first statement, which offers substantial coverage eligible for such provisions.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">While the employer-administered group policy offers $280,000 in combined coverage, only up to $250,000 may be advanced prematurely due to the policy’s acceleration limitations.</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to cap</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 acceleration limit referenced in the second statement may be subject to override or interpretation based on provisions defined in the Master Policy, which takes priority per the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">The Master Policy’s governing terms restrict coverage, and the $250,000 acceleration limit represents one such restriction, aligning with the policy’s rules around benefit disbursement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 maximum acceleration limit may affect the ultimate payout received by Jordan Casey Taylor, who is named as the primary beneficiary of the $280,000 policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 maximum acceleration limit applies specifically to the benefit paid to the primary beneficiary, Jordan Casey Taylor, who is designated as the spouse in the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">While the primary beneficiary is entitled to 100% of the benefit ($280,000), the ability to accelerate up to $250,000 reduces the available balance for eventual payout, creating a trade-off between immediate liquidity and future inheritance.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by payout rule</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="52b0c634-376a-4bbe-a0e1-f374e691f95a">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 maximum acceleration limit applies to claims made under the plan’s living benefits feature, which would affect the distribution to the Taylor Family Revocable Trust should it become the recipient due to the absence of surviving primary beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">limiting factor</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b" target="0fd4ce41-df87-49ef-b846-edcb6c8e3ffc">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 acceleration cap could affect the contingent beneficiary’s eventual receipt of benefits if funds are advanced prior to death, potentially reducing the full $280,000 payout available per the original policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">limiting factor</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="465b2480-11ac-4f59-8d47-22db6d96bc2f" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has maximum acceleration limit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0b67f7ff-5a78-4f44-9219-234c79681070" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is maximum acceleration amount for</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="75066832-a0f2-4a2a-87d6-861339c4a1b3" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is required to qualify for</data>
    </edge>
