    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="f1c23475-745a-4fdf-9a69-a16cf36cb7ae">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">financial value</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="c6d69956-ed9d-4a89-98d0-93030e9fea7a">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">location</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="0953022c-0eee-4dfd-b463-50bc9aab3ace">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">contact info</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="2619808f-2154-4a17-99e9-09638913debc">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">document</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="79a3413d-9cdb-4656-866c-b1e3876ab761">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">document</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="4132a8d1-925a-4d1d-9938-86825d3dcc4d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">document</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="502d1c14-6f95-43e5-b370-377d6996cdc0">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="b8174145-f89d-4f38-960d-be2c2f2bd7ca">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">An actuarial discount applied to the accelerated benefit relies on the presence of group coverage that permits such provisions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="a4f89de4-1afc-4c97-948f-48c37a6cfc59">
      <data key="d3">An actuarial discount reduces the accelerated benefit paid out in advance, lowering the eventual death benefit. This mechanism supports the feature of portability, where no proof of insurability is required, ensuring financial sustainability despite relaxed eligibility conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">An actuarial discount reduces the accelerated death benefit amount, but this only applies once the insured meets the qualifying criteria—such as having a terminal illness with a life expectancy of 12 months or less.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduced by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for an actuarial discount ensures that reducing the final death benefit compensates for the insurer’s loss of investment income from paying out funds prematurely, thus justifying why only a discounted portion of the benefit is paid upfront.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
      <data key="d3">An actuarial discount reduces the amount paid out upon acceleration, ensuring that even the smallest eligible claim ($5,000) reflects this adjustment.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">An actuarial discount reduces the amount payable from the maximum possible acceleration of $250,000, ensuring the final payout reflects financial risk adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="c3c8847b-85e9-4a8d-9b64-6b4b5efd5144">
      <data key="d3">The actuarial discount applied to the accelerated amount ensures it reflects present-value reduction, thereby decreasing the total death benefit available to beneficiaries. This adjustment maintains financial balance in the policy’s payout structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="afec02f1-3018-4d35-a72f-90bd5e82289f">
      <data key="d3">The acceleration of benefits involves an actuarial reduction, but this only applies once the claim process begins, which requires immediate notification from beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The accelerated benefit amount is subject to an actuarial discount, but this occurs only after a claim has been properly submitted through the designated department.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">An actuarial discount adjusts the accelerated payout for terminally ill members, whereas portability enables continuation of coverage after leaving employment—all governed by non-medical requirements and benefit adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The mention of an actuarial discount reducing the accelerated benefit applies specifically to insureds whose coverage was confirmed through documents like the one referenced in fact_sentence_1, ensuring such reductions are based on legitimate, verified policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">The actuarial discount applied to the accelerated benefit depends on the existence of a master group policy governed by the employer, making it relevant to the structural setup described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enabled by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">An actuarial discount on accelerated payments implies a modification to benefit payouts, which falls under the broader scope of terms and conditions defined in the Master Policy governing overall coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">subsumed by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">The actuarial discount reducing the accelerated payout directly influences the net amount paid to the primary beneficiary, Jordan Casey Taylor, upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables beneficiary payout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">The actuarial discount applied to the accelerated benefit determines the net amount payable to Jordan Casey Taylor, who is listed as the spouse and primary beneficiary under the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects beneficiary</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f148ea16-1810-4ee0-8bd3-fc0b480c1222" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">While the primary beneficiary typically receives 100% of the benefit, taking an accelerated payment results in a lower final payout because of an actuarial discount applied to reduce future benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
