    <edge source="72af3f2b-1c51-48ee-8da5-c36c14e9735e" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">The suicide exclusion determines whether a claim is eligible, while the certified death certificate is a mandatory document required regardless of cause of death. One sets a policy restriction, the other enforces administrative compliance.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
