    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">Beneficiary updates managed through HR are possible because the insurance company offers group coverage, providing the framework for employee-related benefits management.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="80ef03d9-a0d8-4e34-b854-917b328e532c">
      <data key="d3">The ability to update beneficiaries at any time implies that the outcome depends on who is alive at the time of death. This leads directly into the scenario described in fact_sentence_2, where lack of living beneficiaries results in the estate receiving the proceeds.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional outcome</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="6158d9a5-ff94-4835-99aa-58729bb45911">
      <data key="d3">The ability to update beneficiary designations at any time enables policyholders to adjust how benefits are allocated, ensuring that unequal distributions can be formally specified rather than defaulting to equality.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="bb3b7a5f-abd9-466a-a39b-019177c58922">
      <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries at any time supports the legitimacy and functionality of the coverage certificate, ensuring it remains accurate and reflective of current intent.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="f2fe91f4-2acc-437e-b04b-0b025b2ef31c">
      <data key="d3">The capability to update beneficiaries at any time relies on the underlying Master Group Policy being active and administered by the employer, making it dependent on the initial policy setup.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="668f2149-7691-4670-aa11-f23fbe2f1f88">
      <data key="d3">While beneficiary updates can occur anytime per the second statement, these actions remain subject to higher-level provisions outlined in the Master Policy, which takes priority over individual certificates.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="70945007-c2b7-452b-9909-9a125e9b73e5">
      <data key="d3">While the master policy governs overall coverage parameters, its allowance for timely beneficiary changes ensures alignment with individual circumstances, reinforcing the practical application of the policy’s administrative guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">The ability to update beneficiary designations anytime enables potential modification of the status assigned to Jordan Casey Taylor in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">The provision permitting beneficiary changes supports the validity and flexibility of designating Jordan Casey Taylor as the spouse beneficiary, ensuring such roles can be adjusted per policyholder intent.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">The ability to update beneficiaries at any time ensures that the intended recipient—the primary beneficiary—is properly identified and eligible to claim the full 100% payout upon event occurrence.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="52b0c634-376a-4bbe-a0e1-f374e691f95a">
      <data key="d3">The policy provision permitting real-time beneficiary changes supports the validity and enforceability of specifying non-primary parties like the Taylor Family Revocable Trust as contingent beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="79accc6d-4303-44fb-afe3-1912cdb727f7" target="0fd4ce41-df87-49ef-b846-edcb6c8e3ffc">
      <data key="d3">The ability to update beneficiaries anytime ensures that the contingent beneficiary named in the original designation—or later assigned—can legally claim the full payout, consistent with the stated 100% disbursement rule.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
