    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is a standard prerequisite for beneficiaries seeking payouts under a group life insurance policy, reflecting the operational requirements tied to the insurer’s coverage framework.</data>
      <data key="d4">required by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is a mandatory step in accessing an accelerated death benefit. This requirement applies specifically to those who qualify due to a terminal illness diagnosis and limited life expectancy.</data>
      <data key="d4">required by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="ad33389a-5e72-4baf-8990-51a347fe4a8a">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is necessary before any claim—including accelerated death benefits—is processed, serving as a foundational step in accessing special provisions like early payouts.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="d03f6263-7bbe-40c1-89fa-5e693533134a">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is necessary to initiate any benefit request, including those involving the minimum $5,000 acceleration. This procedural requirement enables access to accelerated benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="800afedf-6828-402d-ac61-26fa74c9cb5b">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 requires submission of a claim form as part of the process to access benefits. This requirement applies regardless of how much may ultimately be paid out, including the $250,000 maximum mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="6158d9a5-ff94-4835-99aa-58729bb45911">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is a prerequisite step before determining how benefits are allocated among beneficiaries, making it foundational to the execution of the distribution rule.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="afec02f1-3018-4d35-a72f-90bd5e82289f">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a completed claim form is part of the official response to reporting the insured’s death, requiring beneficiary action initiated by immediate notification.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">A completed claim form is necessary to initiate a claim, and it can be acquired through the employer or the insurer, ensuring accessibility for applicants.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that a completed claim form is required, which sets the initial step in the claims process. Fact sentence 2 adds that a certified death certificate is also required, completing the foundational documentation needed before processing can proceed.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e">
      <data key="d3">The completion of a claim form is a prerequisite step before providing proof of beneficiary identity, ensuring procedural order in initiating the claims process.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The completion of a claim form is a prerequisite step before submitting the claim to the designated department. This ensures proper processing once received by Alliance Group Benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="22c4b994-6a5b-49d5-a129-731be848f272">
      <data key="d3">The submission of a completed claim form is a foundational requirement that triggers the processing timeline for benefits. Without it, the insurer cannot begin evaluating or disbursing funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace" target="a4660611-ebc8-4a98-ae71-7b04c1befa54">
      <data key="d3">A completed claim form is necessary to initiate a claim, and it must be sent to the designated mailing address at 1200 Insurance Plaza, Dallas, TX 75201, ensuring proper processing.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
