    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="d8e1336c-f36f-4fab-9741-8b9460ba1e31">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is a mandatory component of the claims procedure, which only applies because the insurance company offers group coverage subject to defined procedures.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is necessary to initiate a claim settlement after the insured’s death. This step follows the event described in fact_sentence_1, where a terminal diagnosis may trigger earlier benefit access, but does not affect its validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">prelude to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="72af3f2b-1c51-48ee-8da5-c36c14e9735e">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is necessary to initiate a claim, even if the death was due to suicide within the exclusion period. This step precedes evaluation of eligibility factors like the suicide clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="80ef03d9-a0d8-4e34-b854-917b328e532c">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is mandatory to begin the claims process, allowing verification of the insured's passing. Without such evidence, even if no beneficiary survives, the estate cannot receive benefits due to lack of processed claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="6158d9a5-ff94-4835-99aa-58729bb45911">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is a prerequisite step before determining how benefits are distributed among named beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="afec02f1-3018-4d35-a72f-90bd5e82289f">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate depends on prior notification of the insured’s death by beneficiaries to initiate the claims procedure.</data>
      <data key="d4">required by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace">
      <data key="d3">The need for a certified death certificate (sentence 2) supports the validity of the claim, which depends on having already submitted a completed claim form (sentence 1). Both elements together constitute core prerequisites for claim initiation.</data>
      <data key="d4">necessitates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that a certified death certificate is mandatory for claiming benefits, reinforcing the necessity of completing the initial paperwork outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate establishes the validity of the insured’s death, which is a prerequisite before verifying who should receive benefits. Proof of beneficiary identity follows as a natural next step to ensure proper disbursement after death confirmation.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="a4660611-ebc8-4a98-ae71-7b04c1befa54">
      <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is one of the documents required to initiate a claim, which must be sent to the designated mailing address for processing.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.8</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">The need for a certified death certificate is a prerequisite for initiating the claims process, which culminates in submission to the designated department.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="22c4b994-6a5b-49d5-a129-731be848f272">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate ensures the legitimacy of the claim, enabling the insurer to begin processing the payment promptly upon receipt.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">Requiring a certified death certificate for claims supports the validity of payouts from individually held policies into which participants have converted from the group plan, ensuring proper verification even when no evidence of insurability was initially required.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">While a certified death certificate is mandatory for initiating a claim, the ability to port coverage without proving insurability ensures continuity of potential benefit eligibility, supporting eventual claim submission even after employment ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">Submitting a certified death certificate is a mandatory part of filing a claim, typically occurring long after employment ends. The timing of this requirement depends on prior actions like portability applications, which must be initiated within 31 days of termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">precondition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
