    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="2cbd5814-f54a-4af1-92c0-18cfd941020d">
      <data key="d3">Beneficiary identity verification is part of the formal claims procedure tied to existing group coverage; without such coverage, this step would not apply.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="89ba6d0e-f1eb-478c-935c-effa8d9500ab">
      <data key="d3">Providing proof of beneficiary identity is a prerequisite step that enables the processing of claims, such as those related to accelerated death benefits under terminal illness provisions.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="6158d9a5-ff94-4835-99aa-58729bb45911">
      <data key="d3">Verifying beneficiary identity ensures that benefits are paid according to the intended distribution, such as equal shares or specific allocations, preventing mispayment.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="afec02f1-3018-4d35-a72f-90bd5e82289f">
      <data key="d3">Verifying beneficiary identity is a critical procedural step that depends on prior notification of the insured’s death, ensuring only rightful beneficiaries proceed with claims.</data>
      <data key="d4">required by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="fabc920e-4e63-48bd-8ae0-5520935f9ace">
      <data key="d3">Proof of beneficiary identity supports the validity of the claim form by confirming who is entitled to benefits, reinforcing the legitimacy of the submission.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="30ed27ef-e97f-4082-96c0-a90281492f8f">
      <data key="d3">Proof of beneficiary identity is a mandatory component of the claim submission, which cannot proceed without first acquiring the claim form from the employer or insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">required by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="6a34626d-60fc-44c8-a650-49df4e862518">
      <data key="d3">Providing proof of beneficiary identity depends on having already confirmed the insured’s death through a certified death certificate. Without this foundational evidence, identifying beneficiaries would be premature or invalid.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="4a5e1799-2abe-49d2-a8ee-2933001fa99f">
      <data key="d3">Verification of beneficiary identity is a prerequisite before submitting a claim, ensuring only rightful recipients access benefits. This step occurs prior to sending documents to the designated department.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
