      <data key="d3">Proof of beneficiary identity ensures eligibility verification before processing begins, enabling prompt handling of claims upon submission of complete documentation.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="a4660611-ebc8-4a98-ae71-7b04c1befa54">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 requires verifying beneficiary identity before initiating a claim, ensuring legitimacy. This requirement complements fact_sentence_2 by establishing a prerequisite step prior to sending documents to the designated mailing address.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ba0648f1-21c7-41d2-baec-33f72f4b198e" target="84ecaece-d3be-49c1-95f0-cc92e7c46732">
      <data key="d3">Verifying beneficiary identity (fact_sentence_2) is critical for distributing funds from a converted policy, especially since such policies are subject to the $200,000 cap outlined in fact_sentence_1, ensuring accurate allocation per the established limit.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
