    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a">
      <data key="d3">Section 11 outlines the premium waiver provision, which requires proof of total disability lasting six consecutive months to activate the benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47">
      <data key="d3">Section 11 outlines the Waiver of Premium provision, which allows for premium payment relief when certain criteria are met—specifically, total disability before age 60. This enables continuation of coverage without additional costs during prolonged disability.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577">
      <data key="d3">Section 11 outlines the Waiver of Premium provision, which enables coverage continuation without premium payments when certain conditions are met, such as total disability.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d3">Section 11 outlines the Waiver of Premium provision, which includes conditions under which it ends; returning to work is explicitly stated as such a condition.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="a70714ad-8510-4e0d-a516-a0551aa2fc77">
      <data key="d3">The Waiver of Premium provision requires annual submission of proof of continued disability to maintain eligibility. Without such documentation, the benefit would not apply even if initial conditions were met.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="06ec4160-b42d-4ff4-aade-db4dc4398172">
      <data key="d3">Section 11 establishes the Waiver of Premium provision, which allows ongoing coverage during total disability. The waiver specifically ends when the individual recovers from disability, ensuring continuity only while incapacity persists.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="be8734b0-e512-496b-b54a-fa04e79d616d">
      <data key="d3">Section 11 outlines the Waiver of Premium provision, which includes the rule that the waiver ends when the insured turns 65. This provides context on how long the benefit lasts based on age.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164" target="58ae820f-579c-44dc-8f5b-8b8c8aabed51">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a waiver of premium provision is subject to interpretation based on California state law, which governs the overall terms of the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">governs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fbec3db3-f17e-4191-8d8b-3ee2e185e65b" target="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is covered by</data>
    </edge>
