    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="5cfcf541-93a3-4733-84ca-06ab13c44382">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">role</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="e7bc0658-4389-49c0-86b3-a7db384fe4c0">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">legal jurisdiction</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164">
      <data key="d3">The rule that premiums may be waived for individuals who become totally disabled before age 60 is formally covered under Section 11, which details the terms and conditions governing such a benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">covers</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a">
      <data key="d3">The eligibility for premium waiver due to pre-age-60 total disability depends on the disability lasting at least six consecutive months, ensuring sustained incapacity beyond a short-term period.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577">
      <data key="d3">The condition of being totally disabled before age 60 triggers a premium waiver, enabling uninterrupted coverage even without ongoing payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="a70714ad-8510-4e0d-a516-a0551aa2fc77">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver triggered by total disability before age 60 requires annual proof of continued disability to remain effective. Without such documentation, the waiver would not persist.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver begins when someone becomes totally disabled before age 60, and it continues until they return to work, at which point the waiver ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="06ec4160-b42d-4ff4-aade-db4dc4398172">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver begins when total disability occurs before age 60, but it terminates upon recovery, ensuring that benefits cease once the qualifying condition no longer exists.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="be8734b0-e512-496b-b54a-fa04e79d616d">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver begins when someone becomes totally disabled before age 60, and it continues until they reach age 65, regardless of ongoing disability status after that point.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="58ae820f-579c-44dc-8f5b-8b8c8aabed51">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver condition described in fact_sentence_1 depends on eligibility criteria potentially shaped by state regulations, such as those specified in California law mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver provision relies on active coverage beginning on June 1, 2024; thus, its applicability hinges on the existence of coverage from that effective date onward.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="c0378a0c-15e9-46db-80c6-212e4003560d">
      <data key="d3">The $12 monthly contribution required for voluntary coverage is subject to being waived under certain disability conditions outlined in the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="c2b096bf-e2af-46ce-9492-7da5270a16a1">
      <data key="d3">A premium waiver due to disability ensures that coverage persists, thereby maintaining the spouse’s potential entitlement to death benefits, assuming no change in beneficiary designations.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">A premium waiver for disability allows continuous coverage, ensuring that the specified benefit payout (as stated in fact_sentence_1) remains available should the insured pass away during the period of waived premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="0fd4ce41-df87-49ef-b846-edcb6c8e3ffc">
      <data key="d3">A premium waiver due to pre-age-60 disability ensures continuous coverage, thereby maintaining the possibility that the contingent beneficiary would receive the full benefit payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The ability to waive premiums due to disability supports sustained coverage during hardship, which complements the option to port coverage after job separation by offering financial relief regardless of employment status.</data>
      <data key="d4">complies with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">While the premium waiver allows uninterrupted coverage during pre-age-60 disability, the portability rule ensures access to individual coverage after leaving employment, regardless of health status; these features serve different transition scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7909904c-9f3e-4120-b1ec-d2a076090f06" target="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is applicable when</data>
    </edge>
