    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="0fb61d44-5bc9-4a23-945d-cec5a551fb86">
      <data key="d3">A six-month continuous period of total disability is required to activate the premium waiver, which indirectly affects when benefits might begin being processed by maintaining active coverage without premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164">
      <data key="d3">The six-month continuous disability period is a key eligibility criterion specified under Section 11's waiver of premium provision.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47">
      <data key="d3">A person who becomes totally disabled before age 60 qualifies for premium waiver only if the disability persists continuously for six months, fulfilling the threshold required by the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577">
      <data key="d3">If total disability lasts for six consecutive months, it triggers eligibility for the premium waiver, resulting in uninterrupted coverage without additional premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="a70714ad-8510-4e0d-a516-a0551aa2fc77">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that total disability lasts six consecutive months enables eligibility for the premium waiver, which triggers the need to submit annual proof of continued disability.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that total disability lasts six consecutive months enables eligibility for the premium waiver, which subsequently ends if the individual resumes employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="06ec4160-b42d-4ff4-aade-db4dc4398172">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that total disability lasts six consecutive months enables eligibility for the premium waiver. This waiver continues until the insured recovers from the disability, at which point it ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="be8734b0-e512-496b-b54a-fa04e79d616d">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that total disability lasts six consecutive months enables qualification for the premium waiver, which continues until the individual turns 65, at which point it automatically terminates regardless of ongoing disability status.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The six-month continuous disability rule determines when the premium waiver takes effect; therefore, its application hinges on the coverage's effective date of June 1, 2024, making that date critical for initiating the waiver process.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="c0378a0c-15e9-46db-80c6-212e4003560d">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver eligibility after six months of total disability may relieve the employee from continuing to pay the $12 monthly fee described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables waiver</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="2a484835-c2d5-4916-aaf4-80a161c5cdca">
      <data key="d3">While the premium waiver for total disability ensures continued coverage despite inability to pay, it operates independently of the conversion privilege; one does not rely on the other but together they enhance overall risk mitigation for individuals facing prolonged incapacity.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for six months of total disability enables premium waivers, which complements porting by ensuring continuous coverage even if premiums cannot be paid, especially relevant when employment ends.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62e84355-9c91-4bbf-8c19-93e57c830bba" target="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
    </edge>
