    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="5cd58bed-bbc8-446f-a408-6106bef3b317">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">termination condition</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="cfba04c1-5881-4d3f-bfa4-f287b6c1e318">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">organization</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="589a82a5-746a-40ab-af78-794f65c49f37">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">role</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="9e3945ba-5036-47f1-98ca-af9b64f17300">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">legal jurisdiction</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="0fb61d44-5bc9-4a23-945d-cec5a551fb86">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage without premium payment during disability ensures that beneficiaries qualify for timely payouts when submitting complete claim documentation.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164">
      <data key="d3">The benefit of continuing coverage without premium payments arises from the Waiver of Premium provision detailed in Section 11.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage without premium payment depends on meeting the eligibility criteria, including becoming totally disabled before age 60.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a">
      <data key="d3">Continued coverage without premium payment occurs only when total disability has been sustained for at least six consecutive months, fulfilling the prerequisite set forth in the earlier statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d3">The continuation of coverage without premium payment during disability relies on maintaining the disabled status; once the individual returns to work, the basis for the waiver is invalidated.</data>
      <data key="d4">terminates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="a70714ad-8510-4e0d-a516-a0551aa2fc77">
      <data key="d3">The policy allows coverage to continue without premium payments when an individual is disabled, but this benefit requires annual verification of ongoing disability through documented evidence.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for verification</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="06ec4160-b42d-4ff4-aade-db4dc4398172">
      <data key="d3">When an insured person is totally disabled, premiums are waived so coverage continues without payment. However, once they recover from disability, the waiver terminates.</data>
      <data key="d4">ends during</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="be8734b0-e512-496b-b54a-fa04e79d616d">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver allows continuous coverage without payment during disability, but it terminates once the insured turns 65, regardless of disability status.</data>
      <data key="d4">terminates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The rule that coverage continues without premium payment during disability relies on the initial effective date to determine eligibility and activation of the waiver provision.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="c0378a0c-15e9-46db-80c6-212e4003560d">
      <data key="d3">The absence of required premium payments during disability allows the employee’s voluntary coverage—currently funded by a $12 monthly payment—to remain active despite non-payment, ensuring uninterrupted benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="2c03a154-97c0-4d73-ad37-1599582fab56">
      <data key="d3">If the insured becomes disabled and qualifies for the premium waiver, coverage continues, preserving the possibility that Jordan Casey Taylor, as the primary beneficiary, could receive the benefit payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="b9fb6a96-3110-4371-bdfa-b3a62b485271">
      <data key="d3">The second fact ensures continuous coverage even during disability, preserving the possibility that the named primary beneficiary could receive the full payout described in the first fact.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="52b0c634-376a-4bbe-a0e1-f374e691f95a">
      <data key="d3">The premium waiver enabling coverage during disability ensures that the policy remains active, thereby preserving the validity of the contingent beneficiary clause naming the Taylor Family Revocable Trust.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="e354fe16-ca2b-40c3-a6a8-b4f688cd15e9">
      <data key="d3">The ability to port coverage relies on timely conversion after leaving employment, while disability-related premium waivers sustain coverage during illness without additional cost—these provisions serve overlapping goals but function independently.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577" target="03d8ddf1-d4d8-4fbc-aa24-7b7db121df87">
      <data key="d3">The ability to maintain coverage during disability via waived premiums supports long-term stability in benefit continuity, aligning with the principle that individuals should retain protections even when unable to pay premiums, including those who later leave employment.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7a2e3036-dd0e-4a35-99fc-e3738b885684" target="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
    </edge>
