    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="be20ea5b-1e30-4df6-875f-f118a70b2164">
      <data key="d3">The end of the premium waiver upon return to work is part of the details covered under Section 11, which governs the Waiver of Premium benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="eaa5dac8-c5eb-44c8-ba4e-507da4e5bf47">
      <data key="d3">A person’s eligibility for a premium waiver depends on being totally disabled before age 60; once they return to work, the waiver terminates regardless of other conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">terminates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="2a19b2b9-fddd-401f-bef2-b20573f7051a">
      <data key="d3">If an individual returns to work, the premium waiver stops, even if the initial six-month disability criterion was met earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">terminates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="c4725b84-8de5-4ef8-a696-eca5ff0b4577">
      <data key="d3">Returning to work directly ends the premium waiver because it indicates cessation of the qualifying disability, thereby reversing the condition that enabled continuous coverage without payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="a70714ad-8510-4e0d-a516-a0551aa2fc77">
      <data key="d3">The cessation of the premium waiver upon return to work implies that continuous verification through annual submissions is necessary to confirm whether the disabling condition persists.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="06ec4160-b42d-4ff4-aade-db4dc4398172">
      <data key="d3">If an individual returns to work, it indicates they have recovered from their disability, thereby terminating the premium waiver. This aligns directly with the condition stated in sentence 2 regarding recovery.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="b8006244-ba88-4c0f-b1d8-4d8125ad2697">
      <data key="d3">The rule that premium waiver ends upon returning to work implies that ongoing coverage from June 1, 2024, may be maintained only during periods of continuous disability, making the effective date critical for determining waiver eligibility and duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="c0378a0c-15e9-46db-80c6-212e4003560d">
      <data key="d3">While the $12 monthly payment covers voluntary coverage, the premium waiver provision allows such payments to cease temporarily if the employee becomes disabled; thus, the financial obligation may pause even though it was previously committed.</data>
      <data key="d4">temporary exemption</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b" target="a53bb99a-3253-4bd8-9b0c-bc4334f7b67d">
      <data key="d3">Returning to work triggers the end of premium waivers, potentially affecting financial capacity to maintain new individual coverage; thus, it influences urgency around initiating portability applications within the 31-day window.</data>
      <data key="d4">timing influence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23d6bafc-2dc9-47c4-b459-9872b5530f09" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">terminates when return to work</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8c1567af-cc00-4e26-b583-2a4f6f51cbfd" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">initiates</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f5e453f9-fc30-414f-acbd-31ca5a13edf0" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">terminates</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9e2c9f8e-dc02-4ca5-9808-6efba93c575f" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has premium waiver terminated upon return to work</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e14105-58dd-431d-af44-db3119a0b6c6" target="23b0d891-5c67-4e52-8ec2-f5323703371b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">govern the conditions for premium waiver termination</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="06ec4160-b42d-4ff4-aade-db4dc4398172" target="218461b1-f541-4868-a754-300884ddb681">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
